From 1348a95a5e68e8ae35927244f9c93bde3e787172 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:59:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution settings: placement of the behaviour of a material

The parameter `BehaviourExecutionLocation` (`cpu` or `gpu`) given to
`addBehaviourIntegrator` places the behaviour of a material, taking
precedence over the execution settings: for instance, one material
integrated on the CPU and the others on the GPU. It is removed from the
parameters given to the behaviour integrator, and checked against the
library as the settings are.

ExecutionSettingsTest: the library of the other processor, refused by the
settings, is accepted with this parameter when a GPU is used (refused
without GPU); without the parameter taken into account, the GPU variants
fail (mutation detected). CPU suite 198/198, GPU variants 20/20.
